course: dictionary
lesson: 4206
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so you must find the right one from the words around it. This is the context. In «The Gospels tell of amazing things Jesus did», the Gospels are books about Jesus, so gospel must mean one of those books.
explain: Capital letters and phrases are clues too. «John's Gospel says Jesus was in the Temple» names one of four books. In «Don't take everything you read online as gospel», there are no books or music, so gospel means something completely true.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If «take it as gospel» means completely true, then «Don't take everything you read online as completely true» still makes sense. That tells you your meaning is right.
fact: Gospel has several meanings, so context tells you which one to use.
fact: The Gospels are the four books of the New Testament: Matthew, Mark, Luke and John. They tell of the life, teaching, death and rising of Jesus.
fact: The gospel is the "good news" of Jesus that Christians share.
fact: Gospel music is a joyful style of Christian music with roots in African American churches. A gospel choir sings with clapping and strong harmonies.
fact: "Gospel truth" or "take it as gospel" means something completely true.
exercise: «John's Gospel says Jesus was in the Temple at the Feast of Dedication.» Here Gospel means | *One of the four books about the life of Jesus | A church building | Something completely true | Joyful music sung by a choir
exercise: «Don't take everything you read online as gospel.» What does gospel mean here? | *Completely true, so you should check it first | Good news about Jesus | A joyful song sung in a choir | A holy book read standing up
exercise: In church the Gospel reading is often read standing up, as a mark of respect. What does Gospel mean here? | A gospel choir singing | A joyful style of music | *One of the four books about the life of Jesus | Something completely true
test: «The gospel is the good news of Jesus that Christians share.» In this sentence gospel means | *The good news of Jesus | A school subject | A quiet prayer | A kind of bread
test: «The gospel choir sang with clapping and strong harmonies.» In this sentence gospel means | *A joyful style of Christian music | A quiet prayer | A church building | A type of bread
exam: Dani reads «The Gospels tell of amazing things Jesus did» and says gospel means joyful church music. What is the right meaning here? | *Books that tell the life of Jesus | A church choir | Joyful music from church | Completely true
